From 06ecb73a087ff672edb7ab2242ebd3715634bbc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 2loch-ness6 <195493188+2loch-ness6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:00:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] firehose: add OPPO/OnePlus VIP (verified image protection)
 support

Newer OPPO/OnePlus/Realme targets (SM8650/OxygenOS 15 and up) enable
OPPO's VIP extension: firehose refuses every storage command until the
host has handed it the signed digest table and signature. With stock
edl.py such a target just fails, e.g. "Failed to open the UFS Device" or
"label cannot be null".

Implement the host side of the handshake:

- --vip, --vip-digest, --vip-sign, --vip-label: the digest table
  (Digest.elf / Digest.mbn) and signature (Sign.bin) files used by the
  official OPLUS tool. Because they apply to every command, they are
  stripped from argv before docopt sees them instead of being added to
  each usage line.
- firehose.connect(): when the target announces VIP with its "receiving
  the partition info of size N" prompt, send the digest table, then
  <verify value="ping" EnableVip="1"/>, then the signature. If any step is
  rejected, mark VIP as failed and refuse to configure the target.
- firehose.parse_vip_table(): parse the SVIP digest table (magic
  0x7CEF0312) into a per-partition map of permissions, start sector and
  size.
- cmd_read(), cmd_read_buffer(), cmd_program(), cmd_program_buffer(),
  cmd_erase(): emit the label= attribute that VIP targets require in order
  to authorise access. It defaults to --vip-label ("PrimaryGPT" for GPT
  reads) and is only emitted on VIP targets, so the XML sent to every
  other device is unchanged.
- --skipinitialread: skip configure()'s initial storage-sector probe.
  configure() itself still has to run, it is what initialises the storage.
- cmd_read_buffer(): use the parsed response dict in the error path
  instead of the legacy tuple indexes. Indexing rsp[2] raised KeyError and
  hid the real target error message. Also stop retrying forever when the
  target stops sending data mid read.
- firehose.connect(): parse every log line of a USB read instead of only
  the first, the remaining lines were dropped.

Verified on a OnePlus 12 (CPH2581, SM8650, UFS, 187 signed digest
entries): target authentication, GPT parsing on all LUNs, reads of
locked and unlocked partitions, and writes to unlocked partitions.
